          transliteration: 'gavyeṣuṇeti yo nityaṃ sāyaṃ prātaratantritaḥ / upasthānaṃ gavāṃ kuryāttasya syustāḥ sadā gṛhe',
          translation: 'The sixty-seven hymns — svddistay — are declared as destroyers of all sins, purifiers and conferrers of welfare. The six hundred and ten hymns of pdvamanye when repeated and used for making oblations will enable one to conquer the dread of death. One should repeat (the hymns) dpohisfha while stand¬ ing in the water to destroy the fear of sin. A man passing through a desert should repeat ( the hymn) pradeuanna after the control (of senses).',
          hindi: '“मेरे पूर्वभागमें चक्रधारी विष्णु एवं दक्षिणपार्श्वमें गदाधारी श्रीहरि स्थित हैं । पश्चिमभागमें शारङ्गपाणि विष्णु और उत्तरभागमें नन्दक-खड्गधारी जनार्दन विराजमान हैं। भगवान् हृषीकेश दिक्कोणोंमें एवं',
          explanation: 'The sixty-seven hymns — svddistay — are declared as destroyers of all sins, purifiers and conferrers of welfare. The six hundred and ten hymns of pdvamanye when repeated and used for making oblations will enable one to conquer the dread of death. One should repeat (the hymns) dpohisfha while stand¬ ing in the water to destroy the fear of sin. A man passing through a desert should repeat ( the hymn) pradeuanna after the control (of senses).',
